WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.840
Here's what to do when a game reacts twice to every press,

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.010
or sees no controller at all.

3
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.930
You're hearing a generated voice.

4
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:11.155
If every press counts twice,

5
00:00:11.525 --> 00:00:15.985
the game reads both your pad and PadForge's virtual controller.

6
00:00:16.025 --> 00:00:17.275
HidHide fixes that.

7
00:00:17.665 --> 00:00:19.705
Open Settings and find the HidHide Driver card.

8
00:00:19.745 --> 00:00:24.915
Install it there if it's missing, and keep Hide Devices from Games on.

9
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:30.640
Then open the Devices page, select your pad, and tick Hide from Games.

10
00:00:32.052 --> 00:00:35.252
A Bluetooth pad that a game or Steam opened first

11
00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:38.392
stays visible to it until the pad reconnects.

12
00:00:38.432 --> 00:00:41.242
Turn the pad off and on, or restart the game.

13
00:00:41.772 --> 00:00:43.682
If Steam starts before PadForge,

14
00:00:44.172 --> 00:00:47.462
turn on Keep Devices Cloaked Between Launches, in Settings.

15
00:00:48.902 --> 00:00:52.032
If a game sees no controller, check the Dashboard.

16
00:00:52.582 --> 00:00:56.352
The controller's flame should be lit, and the engine should say Forging.

17
00:00:57.042 --> 00:01:01.112
Some games look for controllers only when they start, so restart the game.

18
00:01:02.401 --> 00:01:06.501
If the Devices page is empty, try another port or cable,

19
00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:10.431
and connect a Bluetooth pad in Windows before you start PadForge.

20
00:01:12.642 --> 00:01:16.552
Find more fixes under Troubleshooting, at padforge.org.
